Z||000000||REDHOTT88||12-25-2001||11:44 AM||||I was wondering... lately when my 2.8 v6 gets to be warmed up, about 5 minutes, whiteish smoke comes up from under the decklid. <P>Not a whole lot, but enough to worry me.<P>I did just change the oil, about 2 weeks ago, and it does look like oil burning off, but it seems to be coming from under the engine or behind where I can't see..<P>Is my baby gonna blow? Temp guage reads normal 210-230ish. check engine light does not come on, oil level is good.<P>Maybe leaking around oil filter? Suggestions?<P>Guess I might really have a RED HOT 88!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">      <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I><BR><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||LoW_KeY||12-25-2001||12:03 PM||||Valves going bad? I know with my old engine it did that right on start ups and it did it crazy! I was like whoa.. not good.<P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-25-2001||12:23 PM||||hard to say without seeing it.... <P>what does it smell like? (Note: smell only enough to get a whif. That stuff isn't good for you.)<P>Did it do this before the filter change? If no then the filter could well be dripping. The other main thing to check would be valve cover gaskets.<P>coolant could be "simple" as a hose loose. could be freeze plug, head gasket, waterpump, etc...||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-25-2001||12:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>hard to say without seeing it.... <P>what does it smell like? (Note: smell only enough to get a whif. That stuff isn't good for you.)<P>Did it do this before the filter change? If no then the filter could well be dripping. The other main thing to check would be valve cover gaskets.<P>coolant could be "simple" as a hose loose. could be freeze plug, head gasket, waterpump, etc...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Yeah.. I know its not much to go on without seeing.. It smells oily to me, but my sniffer isn't much good anymore. The smoke is more white than blue though.<P>It didn't do before oil change, (I used Mobil 1).<P>The engine seems very hot to touch, but I never really felt it before, so it might be normal.<P>I don't think it's coolant related.<P>I'll check the filter, because I did hand tighten it.. but it felt really snug.<P>Thanks<P>(I'll check back in later, I'm being summoned to the xmas dinner table.. Jeez, some peoples priorities!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">     <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
